                <pb facs="0434" n="1394" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1394"/>

                <head>No. 939.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Baron d’Almeirim to Mr.
                    Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Portugal in the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1888-06-30"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi>
                            30, 1888</date>. (Received July 2.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State</hi>: Under the instruction of
                    my Government, I have to inform you that His Majesty the King of Portugal has
                    declared a blockade, beginning on the 12th instant, of the port of Quissembo, on
                    the west coast of Africa, north of the Ambriz.</p>
                <p>While having the honor to make this communication to you, I beg you, Mr.
                    Secretary of State, to accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Baron d’Almeirim</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Consul in Charge of the Business of the Legation of
                            Portugal.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
